WEBVTT

00:00:00.848 --> 00:00:05.678
Token Weather provides a live, read-only MCP service on
Cloudflare. This recording

00:00:05.678 --> 00:00:10.508
uses a real protocol client with synthetic numbers. We connect
without authentication

00:00:10.508 --> 00:00:15.338
and discover the plan context budget tool. The plugin is still an

00:00:15.338 --> 00:00:16.143
unpublished draft.

00:00:17.972 --> 00:00:23.065
For our first scenario, the reference is one hundred thousand
tokens and

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:28.158
current usage is sixty-five thousand. The server returns thirty-
five thousand tokens of

00:00:28.158 --> 00:00:33.251
headroom, sixty-five percent usage, and Cloudy reference weather.
These are calculations from

00:00:33.251 --> 00:00:34.100
supplied numbers.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:40.487
Next, we keep task context and output reserve separate. Adding
twenty thousand

00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:45.040
for the task and five thousand for output produces ninety
thousand planned

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.592
usage and ten thousand remaining. The plan fits the supplied
reference budget.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:56.067
When current usage already exceeds the reference, remaining room
stays at zero.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:01:00.700
The server reports ten thousand current overage and twenty-five
thousand planned overage.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.560
It does not describe a negative amount as available headroom.

00:01:06.408 --> 00:01:11.122
With assumed growth of ten thousand tokens per turn, the five
totals

00:01:11.122 --> 00:01:15.836
are seventy-five, eighty-five, ninety-five, one hundred and five,
and one hundred and

00:01:15.836 --> 00:01:20.549
fifteen thousand. The reference is crossed at turn four. This is
an

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:24.085
assumed-growth forecast, not a prediction of real platform
compaction.

00:01:25.923 --> 00:01:30.488
An unknown reference remains unknown. The server can still
calculate ninety thousand

00:01:30.488 --> 00:01:35.052
planned usage, but it does not invent remaining room, weather, or
whether

00:01:35.052 --> 00:01:39.236
the plan fits. Account quota and monetary cost are also unknown.

00:01:41.078 --> 00:01:46.453
Finally, a server boundary check sends an unsupported messages
field containing synthetic

00:01:46.453 --> 00:01:51.828
text. The service rejects it without echoing the content. It
accepts bounded

00:01:51.828 --> 00:01:57.203
scalar counts and source labels, not transcripts, local paths, or
credentials. This

00:01:57.203 --> 00:02:00.338
checks server behaviour, not language-model prompt routing.

00:02:02.195 --> 00:02:07.410
This walkthrough demonstrates the deployed MCP connection, five
numeric scenarios, and a

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:12.625
server input boundary. The protocol client shown here is a
recording aid,

00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:17.840
not a shipped ChatGPT widget. The service does not read private
ChatGPT

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:23.055
context or control models and chats. OpenAI domain verification
and MCP scanning

00:02:23.055 --> 00:02:25.662
passed. The plugin remains a draft.

